From e9bb13ae478ad9bde3ef9a1f5dde2366e7678a92 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 01:44:58 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gui tests: cli-update waits for the pill's busy state, not
 150ms
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

What changed: the update subtest clicked the pill, slept a fixed 150ms,
then read "Updating…" off it. The busy state is what that read wants, and
it is painted the frame the click lands (paintCLIButton turns the class
and the words on together); under a full GUI run's load the sleep
overshot — the fake update (700ms in the fixture) had finished and the
pill was gone, so the read sat out its whole 5s on
`.row.agent[data-id="codex"] .ag-up` and the subtest went red (#3473,
chromium). The test now waits for the pill's busy class instead, so the
reads, the svg ring check and the while-busy force click land inside the
run whatever the load. The asserts are unchanged. Test-only; no product
code touched.

Run: node --test internal/gui/tests/cli-update.test.cjs, 10 consecutive
runs, 100/100 green (Chromium + WebKit). With the fixture's update delay
cut to 100ms (injected, not committed) the old flow failed 3/3 with the
reported timeout waiting for that locator and the new one passed 3/3;
putting the sleep back with the same injection failed again, the diff
then being that one line. agent-update-all (18), agent-app-version (16)
and agent-connect (4) still pass, both engines.

Fixes #3473

Generated-by: GLM-5.3-Flash (ZCode)
---
 internal/gui/tests/cli-update.test.cjs | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/internal/gui/tests/cli-update.test.cjs b/internal/gui/tests/cli-update.test.cjs
index 097a9bac..33792fe5 100644
--- a/internal/gui/tests/cli-update.test.cjs
+++ b/internal/gui/tests/cli-update.test.cjs
@@ -127,7 +127,11 @@ for (const engine of (process.env.BROWSER ? [process.env.BROWSER] : ["chromium",
       assert(top > 0, "the list must be scrolled");
       const was = await page.locator(`${row("codex")} .ag-up`).evaluate((b) => b.getBoundingClientRect().top);
       await page.locator(`${row("codex")} .ag-up`).click();
-      await page.waitForTimeout(150);
+      // the busy state, not a fixed wait: the update runs while the pill is
+      // busy, so a sleep could end after it was done and the read sat out
+      // its whole 5s on a pill already gone (#3473); waiting for the busy
+      // class lands the reads inside the run whatever the load
+      await page.locator(`${row("codex")} .ag-up.busy`).waitFor();
       assert.equal(await page.locator(`${row("codex")} .ag-up`).textContent(), "Updating…");
       assert.equal(await page.locator(`${row("codex")} .ag-up.busy`).count(), 1);
       // its ring turns inside the svg, round the viewBox's centre: a turned
